      "ihh:notes": "Sentence from Einstein's letter of 2 August 1939 to President F. D. Roosevelt. The LoC post prints it without the comma after 'However'; the GHDI transcription has 'However, such bombs'. The claim follows the registry-institutional source (LoC). Drafted by Einstein and Leo Szilard per the LoC post.\n2026-10-09 fix round 1 (task 10b review): claim switched from the LoC wording ('However such bombs might very well prove to be too heavy for transportation by air.', no comma) to the letter's wording as transcribed by GHDI (EIN-S-0069), which is the matching evidence quote; the LoC quote (EIN-S-0068) stays as institutional corroboration and covers every word of the claim.\nEdit lock (2026-10-09): claim changed after verification; adversary verdict 'supported' by codex:gpt-5.5 (run adv-20261009T190133-9e8d, 2026-10-09) cleared for re-verification."
