      "ihh:notes": "Journey pin fact for the Washington room. The Evening Star article says 'today'; the page record (EIN-S-0073) dates the page April 25, 1921. OCR reads 'White H<*use'; the Harris & Ewing record EIN-S-0021 names the White House. EIN-S-0021 is dated [between 1921 and 1923] by LoC, so it corroborates the place and the people, not the day. Round 2 (2026-10-10): added EIN-S-0088 (National Archives exhibit caption, a holder other than LoC) as independent corroboration that President Harding received the National Academy of Sciences at the White House in April 1921; it does not name Einstein."
