    {
      "@id": "ihh:EIN-F-0096",
      "@type": "Claim",
      "text": "In 1921, Einstein visited the United States to help raise funds for the Hebrew University in Jerusalem.",
      "about": {
        "@id": "ihh:person-einstein"
      },
      "ihh:category": "work",
      "ihh:eventDate": "1921",
      "ihh:place": "United States",
      "ihh:status": "single-source",
      "ihh:primaryDocument": true,
      "ihh:isDirectQuote": false,
      "citation": [
        {
          "@id": "ihh:EIN-S-0008"
        },
        {
          "@id": "ihh:EIN-S-0089"
        }
      ],
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": [
        {
          "@id": "ihh:EIN-S-0008"
        },
        {
          "@id": "ihh:EIN-S-0089"
        }
      ],
      "ihh:evidence": [
        {
          "ihh:source": {
            "@id": "ihh:EIN-S-0008"
          },
          "ihh:quote": "1921\nAided by his fame, Einstein championed the fledgling German republican government and other liberal causes. Partly as a result of this, he and his theory of relativity came under vicious attack from anti-Semites. He began traveling, attended an International Trade Union Congress in Amsterdam, and he visited the United States to help raise funds for the Hebrew University in Jerusalem.",
          "ihh:locator": "timeline entry 1921"
        },
        {
          "ihh:source": {
            "@id": "ihh:EIN-S-0089"
          },
          "ihh:quote": "Dr. Albert Einstein, propounder\nof the famous theory of relativity,\nlanded In New York the other day. It\nIs his Hrst visit. lie comes to raise\nmoney for the Hebrew university on\nthe Mount of Olives.",
          "ihh:locator": "page OCR text, item 'Dr. Einstein and Relativity'"
        }
      ],
      "ihh:extractor": {
        "ihh:model": "claude:claude-opus-5-5",
        "ihh:runId": "einstein-rooms-2026-10-10",
        "ihh:date": "2026-10-10",
        "ihh:verdict": "supported"
      },
      "prov:wasGeneratedBy": {
        "@id": "ihh:run-einstein-einstein-rooms-2026-10-10"
      },
      "ihh:adversary": {
        "ihh:model": "codex:gpt-6-sol",
        "ihh:runId": "adv-einstein-registry-2026-10-16",
        "ihh:date": "2026-10-16",
        "ihh:verdict": "supported",
        "ihh:quoteInSnapshot": true,
        "ihh:quoteInLive": "unreachable",
        "ihh:entailed": true,
        "ihh:addsInformation": false,
        "ihh:atomic": true,
        "ihh:sourceTypeOk": true,
        "ihh:rationale": "No problem found; the Library of Congress OCR source could not be loaded for a live check."
      },
      "ihh:reviewState": "pending",
      "ihh:review": {
        "ihh:state": "pending"
      },
      "ihh:notes": "The occasion of the 1921 visit. AIP's chronology corroborates the 1921 visit (not the fundraising purpose). Caution from PROPOSED.md: the IAS 'In Brief' page reproduces AIP exhibit text, so the two may be one text. Round 2 (2026-10-10): EIN-S-0059 (AIP chronology) removed from the evidence: EIN-S-0008 (IAS) reproduces the AIP exhibit 'Einstein: Image and Impact' and EIN-S-0059 is a page of the same AIP exhibit, so the two are one text, not two independent holders. Added EIN-S-0089 (Bolivar County Democrat, April 30, 1921, a contemporaneous syndicated report held by LoC) as the independent second source; its OCR reads 'Hrst' for 'first' and 'lie' for 'He'."
    },
