      "ihh:notes": "Journey pin fact for the San Diego room. Date from the LoC record (caption-card data) and the United Press dateline; IAS dates its photograph 1930. Category immigration is the nearest schema category for an arrival by ship; this was a visit, not an immigration.\nEdited 2026-10-10 after the first adversary pass (adv-20261010T165246-4f40): the Imperial Valley Press OCR evidence (EIN-S-0082, manual snapshot) could not be confirmed live by Codex, so it was removed and the claim reworded to the remaining records' words ('arrival', 'debarks'). Needs a new adversary verdict.\nEdited again 2026-10-10 after adv-20261010T165845-1910 (refuted: the earlier wording said Elsa debarked, which no quote states). Now restates the UCLA record (Los Angeles Times photograph) and is corroborated by the LoC record (Einstein & Mrs. Einstein, San Diego, Dec. 31, 1930) and IAS EB 064. IAS EB 064 (browser snapshot) removed from the evidence after Codex could not load it live (adversary unclear); it stays the basis of EIN-F-0098 and EIN-M-0039."
