      },
      "ihh:notes": "CONFLICT for owner decision: IAS (this source, owner of the house since 1986) says purchased 1935 and residence from 1935; the NHL nomination form (EIN-S-0091, primary) and NPS article (EIN-S-0057) say 'In 1936 he purchased 112 Mercer Street' (EIN-F-0106, verified). Not resolved by this run. The same IAS page also says the house was built in 1838 on Alexander Street and moved in the 1870s, while the NHL form says builder and date unknown, probably 1870s or 1880s (not staged).\nRuling 2026-10-17 (owner rule: a primary record decides; CONFLICTS.md): no primary record was found after a hard search (Chronicling America 1935-1936, Daily Princetonian archive behind a bot check, archive.org, Mercer County land records behind registration). Lead: Mercer County Clerk Deed 2663 (recorded 1 or 2 August 1935; buyer named as Elsa Einstein, seller Mary Clark Marden), cited by a Wikipedia article, not read. Per the rule the purchase year is not to be shown on the site until the deed is read; the conflict stays here."
    },
