      "ihh:notes": "Round 9 (globe-to-map, 2026-10-29): the departure leg of the 1933 crossing that ends in EIN-F-0122 (arrived New York on the Westernland, October 17, 1933). The AP text spells the liner 'Western Land'; the claim leaves the ship out (EIN-F-0122 carries it). Same text: his wife 'had embarked at Antwerp' (the liner's earlier port; not claimed for him). A Springfield weekly Republican item (1933-10-19, p. 14) says the Westernland called at Halifax, N. S., on October 15 on the way; not staged. Washington Journal (German-language) 1933-10-13 p. 8 says the same in German; not used (G2 is English-only). Claim reworded before adversary review (2026-10-29): 'On October 7, 1933' failed G2 (the dateline's day and the paper's year are in separate quotes); the dateline gives October 7."
    },
