      "ihh:notes": "Rooms run 2026-10-20 (chapter 6, citizenship). Photo #26 of the registration form (page 55 of the PDF), 2005 or 2009, grayscale scan about 1630 x 1257 px; the form's section 7 describes Courtroom 1 ('Ceremonial Courtroom') in detail (oak wainscot, judge's dais, ceiling), which with the photo is enough to model the room. The form says courtrooms 1, 2 and 3 are original to the 1932 building and the floors hold offices of the U.S. District Court. No source on file says the 1940 ceremony (EIN-F-0051) took place in this building or this room: a reconstruction must be labelled as the Trenton federal courthouse of the U.S. District Court, never as 'the room where'. Rights: no item-level statement; reference only."
