          "ihh:quote": "Hedy left Mandl in 1937 and went to England where she met Louis B. Mayer, a film producer and co-founder of Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer (MGM) studios who got her a ticket to Hollywood",
          "ihh:locator": "Historical, paragraph 1"
        },
        {
          "ihh:source": {
            "@id": "ihh:LAM-S-0013"
          },
          "ihh:quote": "In 1937, she fled to London, where she met Louis B. Mayer, co-founder of Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer (MGM) Studios, who was scouting for European talent, and she signed a contract to work for him in Hollywood.",
          "ihh:locator": "paragraph 6"
        },
        {
          "ihh:source": {
            "@id": "ihh:LAM-S-0014"
          },
          "ihh:quote": "Lamarr reached America via London, where she met Hollywood mogul Louis B. Mayer, who was on the lookout for émigré talent. Either in London or on board the Normandie to America, she signed a contract with Mayer and joined MGM.",
          "ihh:locator": "paragraph 6"
        }
      ],
