      "ihh:notes": "Tour travel leg 1 to 2 (the crossing). The ship's name is not given by any source found. Month conflicts with University of the Pacific chronology ('1849 Spring Leaves Scotland'); kept as each source's own version.\nRuling 2026-10-16 (owner rule: a primary record decides; CONFLICTS.md): departure month. February is contradicted by the primary records: the ship Warren sailed from Glasgow on March 4, 1849 (New York Herald, 11 April 1849, p. 4, Maritime Intelligence; New-York Daily Tribune, same day) and its manifest (NARA M237 roll 78, arrival 10 April 1849, image read by eye, needs a person's confirmation) lists Daniel, Sarah, John and David Muir. Set to conflicting so the February month is not shown; the six-week crossing is kept in the log."
