      "ihh:notes": "Round 9 records (research R9-M-NAI-001, 2026-10-29). Chapter: naismith/birth. Shows: The printed entry: 'NAISMITH, James, prof. physical edn.; b. Almonte, Ont., Can., Nov. 6, 1861; s. John and Margaret (Young) N.; A.B., McGill U., 1887 ...' Holder date: 1928. Resolution: page 2195 x 3038; entry crop 700 x 570. Preview previews/nai-birth-whoswho-1928-entry.jpg sha256 9ff27a011e4e027356abd313ff02d4f4661cf5e5f82947459c97f5e2598b3960. Supports facts: NAI-F-0035. Rights basis: Published in the US in 1928 -> pre-1931 US publication rule. No holder rights statement (IA is not a holder): rests on the owner's pre-1931 rule. A 1928 reference entry, not a record made at the birth. Rights: no holder rights field; the statement is the holder page's own publication date. Owner ruling 2026-10-29: publications before 1931 are public domain wherever published.\nalt_text narrowed on 2026-10-30 to the holder's own words (the adversary found the earlier wording said more than the snapshots show); was: Who's Who in America 1928-1929: Vol 15: James Naismith was born in Almonte, Ontario on November 6, 1861 (NAI-F-0035)."
