      "ihh:notes": "Round 9 records (research R9-M-NAI-009, 2026-10-29). Chapter: naismith/honoured. Shows: The item headed \"Basketball First Day\" in its column; OCR: \"First day ceremonies for the 4-cent Basketball stamp honoring the inventor of the game, Dr. James Naismith, will be held at 10 a.m. tomorrow\" Holder date: 1961-11-05. Resolution: crop region 300,6300,1900,1067 of the page (IIIF https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:ndnp:dlc:batch_dlc_fellini_ver02:data:sn83045462:00280609043:1961110501:0318/300,6300,1900,1067/full/0/default.jpg). Preview previews/nai-honoured-evestar-1961-11-05-p50.jpg sha256 60e640eea1b69391a47d13a588c8da82ccbc8e418214ca1cc7ba4c45127d3174. Supports facts: R9-F-002. Rights basis: LoC Chronicling America page OUTSIDE the ruled 1933-1939 range: needs the owner to extend the 2026-10-27 ruling to this year (brief lists CA pages generally). Shown only after that.  Page snapshot snapshots/loc-sn83045462_1961-11-05_ed-1_sp_50.json.\nrights_url set on 2026-10-30 to the page record itself (was https://www.loc.gov/homepage/legal.html, which does not carry the Chronicling America statement; the statement is on the page record, as on the round-7 pages)."
